1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,884
The AI says the feature is finished.

2
00:00:02,884 --> 00:00:08,548
But someone still has to click, capture the failure, and explain it all again.

3
00:00:08,548 --> 00:00:11,482
Ming gives every done a checkable result.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,450
I open Shipboard, a small task app with a deliberately planted persistence bug.

5
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:25,998
Ming accepts browser-ready HTML, static ZIPs, or public GitHub website folders.

6
00:00:25,998 --> 00:00:28,600
This is my actual uploaded app.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,378
My requirements are simple: reject an empty task, add a named task, and keep it after a refresh.

8
00:00:36,378 --> 00:00:40,587
These expectations become the standard for this run and the next.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,734
I ask Seed two point zero Pro for a checklist.

10
00:00:49,734 --> 00:00:52,833
It reads the requirements and the app structure.

11
00:00:52,833 --> 00:00:58,601
The draft proposes actions and passing conditions; it does not decide the results.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,049
Before anything runs, I review what Ming will do and what counts as passing.

13
00:01:08,049 --> 00:01:10,278
I choose Approve and check.

14
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:14,437
Ming now performs those actions against the app in my browser.

15
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,889
The task appears, but disappears after reload.

16
00:01:23,889 --> 00:01:28,063
That is a real failed check, not a preselected result.

17
00:01:28,063 --> 00:01:33,351
The saved image shows the observed page, alongside the expected behavior.

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,094
I copy instructions for my coding AI.

19
00:01:39,094 --> 00:01:45,167
The brief includes the requirements, exact steps, observed failure, and source identity.

20
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:51,210
Copying does not send anything or repair the code; the coding assistant handles that separately.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,703
I now upload a prepared corrected version and keep the original checklist.

22
00:01:59,703 --> 00:02:02,717
Ming repeats the same browser actions.

23
00:02:02,717 --> 00:02:05,736
This time the task survives the refresh.

24
00:02:05,736 --> 00:02:10,190
The comparison preserves the first failure beside the passing revision.

25
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,973
IBM Bob built Ming's original browser runner, evidence history, model adapter, and repair foundations.

26
00:02:22,973 --> 00:02:25,707
These are the genuine task records.

27
00:02:25,707 --> 00:02:31,600
After Bob's trial quota ended, Codex completed the product and later refinements.

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,809
Passing covers the checks we approved, not every possible behavior.

29
00:02:41,809 --> 00:02:45,848
Ming makes the next AI conversation start with evidence.

30
00:02:45,848 --> 00:02:48,117
Every done comes with proof.
